:"e14bd61049946b018a056a9d07b1d162df1d6b78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commits/e14bd61049946b018a056a9d07b1d162df1d6b78"}],"sha":"62a965429dcf8316e4673afe8e344b8f36867523","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commits/62a965429dcf8316e4673afe8e344b8f36867523"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60376898?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hemant-rao","id":60376898,"login":"hemant-rao","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMzc2ODk4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commits/e14bd61049946b018a056a9d07b1d162df1d6b78/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T20:40:32Z","email":"mrhrao@gmail.com","name":"mrhrao@gmail.com"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T20:40:32Z","email":"mrhrao@gmail.com","name":"mrhrao@gmail.com"},"message":"docs: restructure the README around what a reader is trying to do\n\nThe 1.x README grew section by section and ended up ordered by feature\nrather than by task, with the framework entries and the option table\ncarrying most of the weight. Rewritten so it reads top to bottom:\ntry it, install, the four types, calling, closing and updating,\nconfiguration, then the full option tables grouped by what they affect\n(box, skin, text, long messages, accessibility, methods).\n\nNew sections cover the ground 2.x added and the questions that kept\ncoming back: positions on phones — that the edge stacks merge below\n520px, that notches and home indicators are handled through the safe\narea insets, what is worth setting yourself on mobile, and the one case\nthe merge deliberately does not cover (521–1059px, where three 350px\ntoasts fired on the same edge at once can overlap, exactly as in every\nfixed-position toast library) — plus animations, accessibility, an FAQ,\nTypeScript, and SSR named for the frameworks people actually search for.","tree":{"sha":"5a744126b5942712969ca7853863aaa3116db3a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/git/trees/5a744126b5942712969ca7853863aaa3116db3a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/git/commits/e14bd61049946b018a056a9d07b1d162df1d6b78","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60376898?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hemant-rao","id":60376898,"login":"hemant-rao","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMzc2ODk4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commit/e14bd61049946b018a056a9d07b1d162df1d6b78","node_id":"C_kwDOPiXh4NoAKGUxNGJkNjEwNDk5NDZiMDE4YTA1NmE5ZDA3YjFkMTYyZGYxZDZiNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commit/41864ee2dde99068009be4d86f4d1a25fd0576b5","sha":"41864ee2dde99068009be4d86f4d1a25fd0576b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commits/41864ee2dde99068009be4d86f4d1a25fd0576b5"}],"sha":"e14bd61049946b018a056a9d07b1d162df1d6b78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commits/e14bd61049946b018a056a9d07b1d162df1d6b78"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60376898?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hemant-rao","id":60376898,"login":"hemant-rao","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMzc2ODk4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commits/41864ee2dde99068009be4d86f4d1a25fd0576b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T20:39:58Z","email":"mrhrao@gmail.com","name":"mrhrao@gmail.com"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T20:39:58Z","email":"mrhrao@gmail.com","name":"mrhrao@gmail.com"},"message":"fix: keep phone toasts visible, clear of notches and correctly stacked\n\nThree narrow-viewport / animation defects in the 2.x renderer, all of\nwhich only showed up once toasts went full-bleed or two of them were on\nscreen at the same time.\n\nCollapse the edge stacks below 520px. The phone media block stretches\ntoasts to the full width, which left the three stacks sharing an edge\npinned to the same rect, hiding one another — an app firing top-left and\ntop-right at once looked like it had dropped one. stackKey() now folds\ntop-* into a single \"top\" stack and bottom-* into \"bottom\" there, and\nresyncStacks() re-homes the live toasts when the viewport crosses the\nbreakpoint (matchMedia change listener for the exact frame, debounced\nresize as the fallback). NARROW_MAX is exported from styles.js and\ninterpolated into the media query, so the two halves cannot drift.\n\nRe-homing detaches the toasts, which blurs the focused one and drags the\npointer out of it. Without care that reads as \"the user left\" and\nsilently resumes a deliberately paused countdown, so the resync runs\nbehind a `restacking` flag that the focusin/focusout/mouseleave handlers\nsit out, and it hands focus back afterwards (following the content into\nits new wrapper for the F8-focused stack, whose element does not\nsurvive).\n\nRespect the safe areas. Every edge distance is written twice — the plain\noffset, then the same value widened by env(safe-area-inset-*) — so\nnotched phones clear the sensor housing and the home indicator while\nengines that cannot parse env() reject the second assignment and keep\nthe 1.x geometry. A single calc() would leave those engines with the\nproperty unset, i.e. unpositioned toasts rather than a fallback.\n\nStop a reflow glide stranding a toast one slot low. A CSS animation\noutranks inline styles, so a FLIP glide started while the enter\nkeyframes were still filling was masked as it played and then stranded\nat its inverted offset the moment armEnterCleanup switched the animation\noff. flipStack now settles a finished-but-filling enter animation\nthrough _utmEnterSettle before measuring, and skips inverting anything\nwhose enter animation is still running — its own keyframes already move\nit. This was the intermittent \"toast sits below its slot\" bug.\n\nCSS_REV goes to 4 so a page running two copies picks up the new sheet.","tree":{"sha":"3bb0c8e0eaeb574efb9a2b58cbed9989185829d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/git/trees/3bb0c8e0eaeb574efb9a2b58cbed9989185829d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/git/commits/41864ee2dde99068009be4d86f4d1a25fd0576b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60376898?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hemant-rao","id":60376898,"login":"hemant-rao","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMzc2ODk4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commit/41864ee2dde99068009be4d86f4d1a25fd0576b5","node_id":"C_kwDOPiXh4NoAKDQxODY0ZWUyZGRlOTkwNjgwMDliZTRkODZmNGQxYTI1ZmQwNTc2YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commit/f3944b431d5c2c19b1c721899da6ea24e8e941cd","sha":"f3944b431d5c2c19b1c721899da6ea24e8e941cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commits/f3944b431d5c2c19b1c721899da6ea24e8e941cd"}],"sha":"41864ee2dde99068009be4d86f4d1a25fd0576b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commits/41864ee2dde99068009be4d86f4d1a25fd0576b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60376898?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hemant-rao","id":60376898,"login":"hemant-rao","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMzc2ODk4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hemant-rao","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hemant-rao/universal-toast-message/commits/f3944b431d5c2c19b1c721899da6ea24e8e941cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:32:18Z","email":"mrhrao@gmail.com","name":"mrhrao@gmail.com"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:32:18Z","email":"mrhrao@gmail.com","name":"mrhrao@gmail.com"},"message":"feat!: framework-agnostic rewrite — Vue, React, Angular and vanilla JS\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the package is now ESM-only and ships an exports map;\ninternal class names moved from toast-* to utm-*.\n\nThe Vue single-file component is replaced by a vanilla-JS DOM renderer, so\nthe library no longer depends on any framework at runtime. Thin adapters sit\non top of it and are published as subpath entries:\n\n  .         core + the Vue 3 plugin (default export)\n  ./vue     the same plugin plus the $toast type augmentation\n  ./react   toast + a render-less <Toaster/>\n  ./angular ToastService / toastService / provideUniversalToast()\n\nvue and react are optional peer dependencies; the Angular entry imports\nnothing from @angular/core, so installing the package never pulls a\nframework a consumer does not use.\n\nThe public API is unchanged: the same positional and object argument forms,\nthe same helpers, and defaults that reproduce the 1.x look pixel for pixel.\nEverything new — other positions, shadows, accent bar, background images,\nother animations, update-in-place by id — is opt-in.\n\nAlso in this release:\n\n- src/renderer.js: the show/hide lifecycle, FLIP reflow glides, pause\n  bookkeeping (hover, keyboard focus, window blur), Escape dismiss, the F8\n  stack hotkey, screen-reader live regions, the See more clamp toggle and\n  update-in-place. Internal paths hold toast references rather than ids so a\n  replacement toast can never act on its exiting twin.\n- src/styles.js: the structural stylesheet as a string, injected lazily on\n  the first show with an optional CSP nonce, versioned by CSS_REV so two\n  copies of the package on one page arbitrate to the newest sheet.\n- Theming stays CSSOM-only (inline custom properties), which keeps it exempt\n  from style-src restrictions under a strict CSP.\n- SSR-safe: nothing touches the DOM at import time and every helper returns\n  -1 without a document.\n- README rewritten end to end, with quick starts for all four targets and a\n  migration section for 1.x users.","tree":{"sha":"8ef7843ca93a88ce3bb55be653dbc14f46f5da60","url":"https://api.gi