ttps://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/ee9c7f7996309eaec19914432e6308d95c2e94e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:33:14Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:33:14Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Retry the first Discord login, and fail fast on a bad token\n\nA host that starts the process before its network is up failed the gateway\nhandshake once and exited, so the bot stayed down until someone restarted it by\nhand. The first login now retries five times with exponential backoff.\n\nA rejected token or an intent the application has not enabled is not retried:\nit fails identically on every attempt, so retrying only delays the operator\nseeing the real reason. `isFatalLoginError` draws that line, and a bad token\nexits immediately with `TokenInvalid` on the first line.\n\nVerified against the live token: the gateway reaches READY and the log is clean\nwith DEBUG=bot:* on. A deliberately bad token exits at once with no retry.\nFull suite: 327 tests, 285 pass, 0 fail, 42 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"88b7d3774e7c095e016fd6b699c1be91f77027cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/trees/88b7d3774e7c095e016fd6b699c1be91f77027cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/commits/ee9c7f7996309eaec19914432e6308d95c2e94e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/ee9c7f7996309eaec19914432e6308d95c2e94e3","node_id":"C_kwDOPjAFOtoAKGVlOWM3Zjc5OTYzMDllYWVjMTk5MTQ0MzJlNjMwOGQ5NWMyZTk0ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/b3dcddfee9ad0b445ca84b80de978bf53b0315eb","sha":"b3dcddfee9ad0b445ca84b80de978bf53b0315eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/b3dcddfee9ad0b445ca84b80de978bf53b0315eb"}],"sha":"ee9c7f7996309eaec19914432e6308d95c2e94e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/ee9c7f7996309eaec19914432e6308d95c2e94e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/b3dcddfee9ad0b445ca84b80de978bf53b0315eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:26:25Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:27:49Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Give the bot a real startup and gateway log, and accept token aliases\n\nThe bot printed nothing about its own connection, so \"the bot is silent\" was\nindistinguishable from \"the process never started\" — the exact ambiguity that\nmade a dead host look like a code fault.\n\nIt now prints a startup banner naming the token variable that won and the\nintents requested, and logs every gateway transition: shard ready, reconnecting,\nresumed, disconnected with its close code, and errors. The ready line names the\naccount and the guilds, which is what tells an operator the process reached\nDiscord at all. Verbose per-event detail goes through `debug` under `bot:*`,\nenabled with BOT_DEBUG or DEBUG.\n\nThe token is read from the first of DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN, BOT_TOKEN, DISCORD_TOKEN,\nTOKEN, CLIENT_TOKEN that is set. Hosts label their secret fields differently and\na bot that will not boot over a naming difference is a needless outage; the\nbanner reports which name supplied it, because with five candidates \"the token\nis set\" does not identify a host that injected the wrong one.\n\nLogging a token is a credential leak, so `redactToken` strips it by value and by\nshape — the shape match covers a token that arrived under a name this process\nnever read — and `guardConsole` wraps the console methods so discord.js''s own\nwarnings and stack traces are covered. discord.js already censors the signature\nin the `Provided token:` line, so this is a second layer. The tests use a\nsynthetic token with the real shape, never a live one.\n\nAlso adds GuildMembers to the requested intents (the application has it enabled)\nand bounds the message/member caches, which a long-lived process otherwise grows\nwithout limit.\n\nVerified against the live token: the gateway reaches READY, the bot is in 2\nguilds, and no token appears in the log with DEBUG=bot:* on. Full suite: 324\ntests, 282 pass, 0 fail, 42 skipped (the skips need a database).","tree":{"sha":"5e22e9598de9dcb76ab55ef71b9e18db6bacb933","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/trees/5e22e9598de9dcb76ab55ef71b9e18db6bacb933"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/commits/b3dcddfee9ad0b445ca84b80de978bf53b0315eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/b3dcddfee9ad0b445ca84b80de978bf53b0315eb","node_id":"C_kwDOPjAFOtoAKGIzZGNkZGZlZTlhZDBiNDQ1Y2E4NGI4MGRlOTc4YmY1M2IwMzE1ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/51f1eecb54c036eafc902f65b0c2bcc47d7a6a33","sha":"51f1eecb54c036eafc902f65b0c2bcc47d7a6a33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/51f1eecb54c036eafc902f65b0c2bcc47d7a6a33"}],"sha":"b3dcddfee9ad0b445ca84b80de978bf53b0315eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/b3dcddfee9ad0b445ca84b80de978bf53b0315eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/51f1eecb54c036eafc902f65b0c2bcc47d7a6a33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T08:26:37Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T08:26:37Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Make admin Discord link-only, and report bot liveness\n\nDiscord was already a link rather than an admin sign-in, but the dashboard\ncould not tell a running bot from a configured-but-dead one: the status\nendpoint reported DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN from the *web* deployment''s environment,\nwhich stays true while the bot host is down. That is the state where nothing\nanswers &dev while the page looks healthy.\n\nThe bot process now stamps bot_settings.last_seen_at on its own one-minute\ninterval — deliberately not the usage poll''s, whose 15-minute default would\nlook stale against the five-minute threshold — and the dashboard shows a \"Bot\nprocess\" tile plus an actionable warning. A bot that has never started reports\nlastSeenAt: null rather than an arbitrary age.\n\nAlso carries the earlier admin Discord diagnostics, the mail ordering fix, and\nthe Docker test-runner documentation.","tree":{"sha":"7592a2c5cc0b2e89dc9cec50a51a598ef656c58c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/trees/7592a2c5cc0b2e89dc9cec50a51a598ef656c58c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/commits/51f1eecb54c036eafc902f65b0c2bcc47d7a6a33","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agen