,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/f37c44d0f70f61c95d05c00e646b9e033a332190/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T09:18:31Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T09:19:12Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Fix the test router''s middleware spread, and test it the way the app calls it\n\n/api/admin/* failed to load with:\n\n  TypeError: function is not iterable (cannot read property Symbol(Symbol.iterator))\n    at buildTestRouter (api/_lib/suite-runner.js:188:44)\n\nrequireAuth is a single middleware function; requireRole is a factory that\nreturns one. The routes spread both, but a spread of a function, not an array,\nthrows before the router is built, so the whole admin function died at load.\nMail and bot routers already pass these as plain values; this now matches them,\nbuilding the owner guard once as requireOwner.\n\nThe tests did not catch it because they passed an array for requireAuth, which\nis not the shape the app passes. A stub that does not match the real interface\ncan only test the stub. They now use a function and a factory, assert the guard\norder on every route, and reject a spread outright.\n\nThe strongest guard is new: tests/admin-test-runner.test.mjs imports the real\napi/admin/index.js in a child process, exactly as the serverless runtime does. I\nconfirmed it fails with the original TypeError when the spread is re-added, and\npasses otherwise. Source-grep assertions could never have caught this, because\nthey only proved the text was present, not that the module loads.\n\nFull suite 300 tests, 259 pass, 41 skipped, 0 fail. tsc and build clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>","tree":{"sha":"7b6e232abd1d613d5e9603fb6d9af4f1c772c747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/trees/7b6e232abd1d613d5e9603fb6d9af4f1c772c747"},"url":"https://api.gi