ttps://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/5791ad21b3d2cf9b6818e90ed11412453ccd1acb","node_id":"C_kwDOPjAFOtoAKDU3OTFhZDIxYjNkMmNmOWI2ODE4ZTkwZWQxMTQxMjQ1M2NjZDFhY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/ec19a2c9267c3cf76322abd6d510fe1c06421550","sha":"ec19a2c9267c3cf76322abd6d510fe1c06421550","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/ec19a2c9267c3cf76322abd6d510fe1c06421550"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/38a962984936ec92f0d48d2b3eda20d20334248f","sha":"38a962984936ec92f0d48d2b3eda20d20334248f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/38a962984936ec92f0d48d2b3eda20d20334248f"}],"sha":"5791ad21b3d2cf9b6818e90ed11412453ccd1acb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/5791ad21b3d2cf9b6818e90ed11412453ccd1acb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/38a962984936ec92f0d48d2b3eda20d20334248f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:14:15Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T16:14:15Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Measure Neon usage org-wide and add an admin test-runner console\n\nThe usage alert now sums every project in the organization by default, which\nis what an usage-based Neon plan bills. NEON_PROJECT_IDS narrows the scope and\nNEON_PROJECT_ID still selects a single project, so neither is required any\nmore. The read follows pagination to the end, because a partial page would\nsilently under-report, and the per-project breakdown is carried into the embed\nand the usage preview. The tier limits are documented as organization-wide\nceilings rather than per-project ones.\n\n/pbad/tests (owner only) runs the repository''s test folder and shows the TAP\nsummary. It is the only route that spawns a process, so the argument list is a\nliteral, no request field is read, and the spawn uses shell: false. One run at\na time is enforced, and a missing tests/ folder reports 503 rather than a spawn\nerror. The child drops NODE_TEST_CONTEXT/NODE_TEST_WORKER_ID so a nested runner\nstill emits TAP when the endpoint is exercised from the suite.\n\nTests cover the org-wide scope, pagination, the env-var narrowing and the\ntest-runner guardrails. Full suite: 292 tests, 251 pass, 41 skipped, 0 fail.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>","tree":{"sha":"12da9869e3988ebb