.com> 1790265381 +0600\n\nMerge pull request #21 from ProjectHub-fie/feat/client-account-pages-discord-linking\n\nAdd client account pages, Discord account linking, and fix mail push delivery","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtUglCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA72kQAK4gbg/ZAqwRHvNRysBHzxMD\n/HFjIV2a/Rl6+Iu7uEjcNvgDpwW2phmE8by9jhq2SfRieydICXchz8kHR8IpXlzt\nx8bnWccY1O8Lwv1v+a1oBSRfXqlNpa6FLxE58oSv87h4sQaK7pb/RfVy+lEDf6oQ\n1FvLYkr1XQRmA8DZIFbLYX/I0ha4OrI5aYVToHIf90viCJ+PwsFeqchGdPQQT/Vf\nRvpWcNd5pVyETvGTKM9VbRld5j4RgOhGmJ7LP51dDbiu5+r53Fsh/rdbxH8AIcIW\nRi5gxsJ68JKeaLRHj6aowS7RnNdESvnggjOVTsphbDqqBPSaDyhMPe/8eYVqDJmR\n7ZGCjxJ+s3i3WAPtHdR381AnPwYw6sJb93Kpdlnanx57Pn9z2AFhHkzYhIEi+CTk\ndvwKrY/7vn5cBkwJYs68x1WBEFeCgbpjXk/dO9AtT+qpYe/1OaL8uyxpb14aYhuJ\nvzqm4ltjC3bJkHjy83CsSnuf59V4cV3tumZ7cd8qsG8xP6vkgB4QDz+K80+7UFnN\nzY3z58dSUPIrIEmQllNdxwI8+ELL+U1OxF+y9IQtMKJe1Tz9bM4JVrkzfwWQXFmH\n8ghokpninZ1YLEI7vKtctI285vtE+VjAO2NuqN7Qon4QSFdiLsI68n03/nbspEl8\nptSAwO9X35DQp/ValK2O\n=W1LN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T15:56:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/ec19a2c9267c3cf76322abd6d510fe1c06421550","node_id":"C_kwDOPjAFOtoAKGVjMTlhMmM5MjY3YzNjZjc2MzIyYWJkNmQ1MTBmZTFjMDY0MjE1NTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/53c3ef7ef37abb5029b6368e42f5c940dc55b2cb","sha":"53c3ef7ef37abb5029b6368e42f5c940dc55b2cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/53c3ef7ef37abb5029b6368e42f5c940dc55b2cb"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/5681742c25d2b1a5c0e3e01b841588fff2c52d28","sha":"5681742c25d2b1a5c0e3e01b841588fff2c52d28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/5681742c25d2b1a5c0e3e01b841588fff2c52d28"}],"sha":"ec19a2c9267c3cf76322abd6d510fe1c06421550","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/ec19a2c9267c3cf76322abd6d510fe1c06421550"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/5681742c25d2b1a5c0e3e01b841588fff2c52d28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:48:03Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:48:03Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Fix Vercel deploy: move shared helpers to api/_lib\n\nVercel turns every file under api/ into a Serverless Function, and the plan\nallows 12. The branch pushed api/ from 10 files to 15 -- api/lib/push.js from\nthe mail fix plus four bot helpers -- so the deploy failed with \"exceeded the\nlimit\". The five new files were helpers, not endpoints; only api/index.js and\napi/admin/index.js are real handlers.\n\nVercel skips a path under api/ that contains /_, /. , /node_modules/ or ends\nwith .d.ts (verified in the installed CLI, detectBuilders). Renaming the\ndirectory to api/_lib takes all 13 helpers out of the count at once and keeps\nevery filename readable, rather than prefixing each file individually or moving\nthem outside api/ where the \"shared helper in api/\" convention would be lost.\n\napi/ now deploys 2 functions, down from 15.\n\nReferences updated across all three consumers: the two functions (''./_lib'',\n''../_lib''), and the Express dev server and bot process (''api/_lib''). Comments,\nAGENTS.md, bot/README.md and verify-deployment.js follow the new path.\n\nAlso removes api-dist/, unreferenced orphaned build output that held a stale\ncopy of the old api/lib tree and was at risk of being misread as functions. It\nis added to .vercelignore so it does not come back.\n\ntests/deployment-limits.test.mjs re-implements Vercel''s detection rule and\nasserts the count, that only the two endpoints are functions, that the helpers\nstill exist under _lib, that no bare lib/ import remains, and that the modules\nstill import. A helper dropped into api/ now fails in CI instead of in a deploy.\n\nSuite: 223 pass, 0 fail. tsc, build, and both entry points verified to load.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>","tree":{"sha":"646207f148f3c7c43d8b239e405e2bc7d005b06c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/trees/646207f148f3c7c43d8b239e405e2bc7d005b06c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/commits/5681742c25d2b1a5c0e3e01b841588fff2c52d28","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/5681742c25d2b1a5c0e3e01b841588fff2c52d28","node_id":"C_kwDOPjAFOtoAKDU2ODE3NDJjMjVkMmIxYTVjMGUzZTAxYjg0MTU4OGZmZjJjNTJkMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/689adc73caca55ef9b23e8f3e1662a06a2a57b3a","sha":"689adc73caca55ef9b23e8f3e1662a06a2a57b3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/689adc73caca55ef9b23e8f3e1662a06a2a57b3a"}],"sha":"5681742c25d2b1a5c0e3e01b841588fff2c52d28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/5681742c25d2b1a5c0e3e01b841588fff2c52d28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/689adc73caca55ef9b23e8f3e1662a06a2a57b3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T08:40:22Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T08:40:22Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Add the ProjectHub Discord bot: usage alerts and &dev role lookup\n\nA private server bot with an `&` prefix, configured from the admin portal.\n\nRuntime split\n-------------\nbot/index.js holds a persistent Discord gateway connection, which a Vercel\nfunction cannot: the function is request-scoped and capped at 30s. So the bot\nruns as its own process (npm run bot) on any long-lived host, and is deliberately\nabsent from vercel.json. Only the control plane is serverless. Nothing under api/\nimports discord.js, so it is not pulled into a function bundle. Shared rules live\nin api/lib so both halves use one definition.\n\nNeon usage alert\n----------------\nReads Neon''s consumption_history/v2 endpoint and posts an embed to the configured\nchannel and webhook when a metric crosses its tier threshold. Neon reports what\nwas consumed, not the plan ceiling, so the limits are configured in the dashboard\nand default to the Free tier. evaluateUsage grades each metric and the worst sets\nthe overall level; shouldAlert then applies a per-metric cooldown, held in\nbot_alert_state, so a sustained overage does not post on every poll.\n\nDelivery goes to the channel and the webhook independently, and only metrics that\nactually reached a destination record their timestamp -- a total delivery failure\nretries next poll instead of being marked sent. The webhook embed pins\nallowed_mentions to an empty parse, since a webhook post can otherwise ping roles.\nOne metric failing to read does not lose the poll: it is reported as unavailable\nand treated as zero.\n\n&dev\n----\nResolves the caller''s Discord id against admin_credentials.discord_id first and\nusers.discord_id second, because one Discord account can be linked to either\nportal; an account linked to both reports both, and a blocked client is reported\nas blocked rather than unlinked. The admin PIN is never selected or rendered: the\nreply lands in a public channel and the PIN is half of the admin login credential.\n\nMentions are handled alongside the prefix, because members treat an @ as \"talk to\nthe bot\"; a bare mention answers &dev. An unknown command is answered only when\nthe bot was addressed directly, so ordinary chatter containing the prefix stays\nsilent.\n\nAdmin portal\n------------\nNew /pbad/bot page (owner/admin only, the same requireRole(''admin'') rule as mail,\nenforced by the router and not just hidden in the sidebar) with a Bot entry in\nthe workspace nav. It edits the prefix, destinations, threshold, cooldown and\ntier limits, and shows runtime readiness for the env vars. A \"Check usage now\"\naction reads the live figures and shows what the alert would decide without\nsending, which tells \"the bot is silent\" apart from \"usage is genuinely low\".\n\nSecrets are environment-only and never stored or returned: DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN and\nNEON_API_KEY. The webhook URL is a credential, so it is stored but masked on read\nby getBotSettingsForDashboard.\n\nTests: new tests/discord-bot.test.mjs (34) covers prefix parsing, role\nresolution, threshold grading, cooldown gating, embed shape, secret masking and\nvalidation, and the dashboard wiring. Full suite passes; tsc and build clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>","tree":{"sha":"1aabf22f2553da6a7e8deeeff63d018148389623","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/trees/1aabf22f2553da6a7e8deeeff63d018148389623"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/commits/689adc73caca55ef9b23e8f3e1662a06a2a57b3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/689adc73caca55ef9b23e8f3e1662a06a2a57b3a","node_id":"C_kwDOPjAFOtoAKDY4OWFkYzczY2FjYTU1ZWY5YjIzZThmM2UxNjYyYTA2YTJhNTdiM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/7901b6a782d7550cf73daf432306040bd4688921","sha":"7901b6a782d7550cf73daf432306040bd4688921","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/7901b6a782d7550cf73daf432306040bd4688921"}],"sha":"689adc73caca55ef9b23e8f3e1662a06a2a57b3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/689adc73caca55ef9b23e8f3e1662a06a2a57b3a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/7901b6a782d7550cf73daf432306040bd4688921/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T08:29:39Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T08:29:39Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Add client account pages and Discord linking, fix mail push delivery\n\nClient dashboard gains two signed-in-only pages:\n\n- /client_profile edits the profile picture, name and email. The email is\n  re-validated with the same rule the register form uses, since a profile\n  update must not be a way around the registration check. Because the address\n  is embedded in the signed session token, the server re-issues the token on a\n  change and the client stores the replacement.\n- /settings links or unlinks Discord, sets or changes the password, and deletes\n  the account. Both new pages appear in the client sidebar only while signed\n  in, with the signed-in email shown the way the admin portal shows it.\n\nAuth rules enforced on both backends (api/index.js and server/routes.ts):\n\n- A password account and a Discord login that only share an email are separate\n  identities. Signing in with Discord against an existing password account is\n  refused as account_exists_requires_link; the account must link from settings.\n- The link is proved by the OAuth handshake with mode=link. The stored Discord\n  id always comes from Discord''s profile response, never from the client.\n- A Discord-only account may set a password, and cannot unlink Discord before\n  it does, so it is never left unreachable.\n\nAdmin portal gets the same treatment: a /pbad/settings page that links and\nunlinks Discord, a Settings entry in the dashboard sidebar, a Continue with\nDiscord button on the admin login screen, and admin_not_linked error reporting.\nOnly an admin row that already carries the Discord id may sign in that way.\ndiscord_id gains a unique index for deployments that predate the column.\n\nMail notifications: inbound mail wrote in-app rows but never delivered a\nbrowser push. api/lib/push.js now fans out to the subscriptions stored for the\nrecipients a notification targets, filtered by each admin''s desktop preference;\ndelivery is best-effort and stale subscriptions are pruned. The client\nregisters the service worker and persists a subscription from both UI paths\nthat enable desktop alerts. VAPID keys are required for real delivery.\n\nTests: new tests/account-settings.test.mjs pins the pages, the sidebar, the\nlink rule and both backends'' enforcement. tests/mail-api.test.mjs gains push\ndelivery coverage. Full Node suite passes.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>","tree":{"sha":"3d2bc4aaa98c8199f1bf29025bb7891cdc65be22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/trees/3d2bc4aaa98c8199f1bf29025bb7891cdc65be22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/commits/7901b6a782d7550cf73daf432306040bd4688921","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-