"subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/c8dadaad406e8616ce02b4ff680bb9bd0a1617c6","node_id":"C_kwDOPjAFOtoAKGM4ZGFkYWFkNDA2ZTg2MTZjZTAyYjRmZjY4MGJiOWJkMGExNjE3YzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/27aa9b6fe0704aabde16f391a67c96763e03220f","sha":"27aa9b6fe0704aabde16f391a67c96763e03220f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/27aa9b6fe0704aabde16f391a67c96763e03220f"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/dd20aeab29ef8de4564eca739d330ccf0e0b993a","sha":"dd20aeab29ef8de4564eca739d330ccf0e0b993a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/dd20aeab29ef8de4564eca739d330ccf0e0b993a"}],"sha":"c8dadaad406e8616ce02b4ff680bb9bd0a1617c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/c8dadaad406e8616ce02b4ff680bb9bd0a1617c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/dd20aeab29ef8de4564eca739d330ccf0e0b993a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T05:35:28Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T05:35:28Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Fix Mailjet false success and the Postgres SSL-mode warning\n\nMailjet now reports success only when Mailjet actually accepts the message:\n\n- validateMailjetMessage rejects a missing/invalid recipient, sender or\n  subject, or an empty body, before any request is posted.\n- mailjetSend logs whether each key is configured, the recipient and the\n  sender before the request, and the HTTP status plus parsed response after\n  it (never a key value, the Authorization header or a token).\n- Add POST /api/admin/mail/mailjet-test, behind the same owner/admin mail\n  guard, plus a Diagnostics tab that sends one real message and reports\n  Mailjet''s acceptance rather than claiming delivery.\n\nThe 200-with-nothing-queued, per-message-error and Sandbox-mode shapes were\nalready treated as failures; this keeps that intact and adds the transport\ndiagnostics and validation around it.\n\nRewrite sslmode=prefer/require/verify-ca to verify-full in\nnormalizeDatabaseUrl. pg-connection-string already treats those three as\naliases for verify-full but warns about them, and the warning reads like a\nconnection failure when it is not. The function moves to api/lib/db-url.js\nso modules that must not open a pool can share it.\n\nCo-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>","tree":{"sha":"882958e14fd719861fdb29d6c9a73bd6840f8772","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/trees/882958e14fd719861fdb29d6c9a73bd6840f8772"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/commits/dd20aeab29ef8de4564eca739d33