url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/1280da8a8b6b57fe2aba8c63f69f46053e233db0","node_id":"C_kwDOPjAFOtoAKDEyODBkYThhOGI2YjU3ZmUyYWJhOGM2M2Y2OWY0NjA1M2UyMzNkYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748","sha":"b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/30cf93e751a8fb245f8e9d804dd8747880aced73","sha":"30cf93e751a8fb245f8e9d804dd8747880aced73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/30cf93e751a8fb245f8e9d804dd8747880aced73"}],"sha":"1280da8a8b6b57fe2aba8c63f69f46053e233db0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/1280da8a8b6b57fe2aba8c63f69f46053e233db0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/7d2afe2004ce07cde2ea0a7cd4721acdf78cc667/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T10:03:17Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T10:03:17Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Fix auth failures across the client and admin portals\n\nAudited both auth paths against a live database and fixed what the audit\nturned up. Every fix has a regression test.\n\nClient sessions were the worst of it. /api/auth/me can only identify a\nuser from the X-User-Session token, and register signed one and returned\nit, but the hook never stored it. A new account appeared signed in from\nlocalStorage and went anonymous on the next load. The same block also\nleft a stale token behind when registration failed.\n\nLogin and register were unreachable whenever Turnstile was unconfigured.\nThe server treats a missing TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY as \"captcha disabled\",\nbut the page fell back to Cloudflare''s test site key and gated submit on\n`!captchaToken` regardless, so the buttons sat disabled with no widget\nreturning a token. The gate is now `captchaRequired`, derived from\nVITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY, and the widget renders only when configured.\n\nTokens never expired. The signed payload carried no exp, so a token\nlifted from a browser was replayable forever and there was no way to end\na session short of rotating SESSION_SECRET for every user at once. The\npayload now carries iat/exp (30 days, SESSION_TTL_DAYS) and the read path\nenforces it. Tokens issued before this change carry no exp and are\nrejected, so existing clients sign in again.\n\nThe admin dashboard shipped a literal session secret,\n''fallback-secret-key-for-vercel'', as a fallback. It is in this public\nrepository, so a deployment that started without SESSION_SECRET let\nanyone who read the source forge a session cookie and reach admin data\nwith no PIN. It now refuses to start instead.\n\nLogin failures were undiagnosable on both portals. /api/auth/login and\nregister answered \"Login failed\", and the admin login \"Internal server\nerror\", for any database fault - which is exactly what a wrong creds\nerror in SESSION_SECRET or DATABASE_URL looks like from outside. All\nthree now return describeDbError(), which maps known Postgres codes to a\nshort message and never leaks the connection string or bound parameters.\n\nAlso dropped debug logging that printed the loaded user to the console.","tree":{"sha":"1f23c437524f3c68daf40dc526dcf5ee79aa6505","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/trees/1f23c437524f3c68daf40dc526dcf5ee79aa6505"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/commits/7d2afe2004ce07cde2ea0a7cd4721acdf78cc667","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/7d2afe2004ce07cde2ea0a7cd4721acdf78cc667","node_id":"C_kwDOPjAFOtoAKDdkMmFmZTIwMDRjZTA3Y2RlMmVhMGE3Y2Q0NzIxYWNkZjc4Y2M2Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748","sha":"b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748"}],"sha":"7d2afe2004ce07cde2ea0a7cd4721acdf78cc667","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/7d2afe2004ce07cde2ea0a7cd4721acdf78cc667"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/30cf93e751a8fb245f8e9d804dd8747880aced73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:38:07Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:38:51Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Match the client sidebar to the admin sidebar\n\nThe two sidebars were meant to share one visual language and the shared sidebar\ntokens in index.css already agreed, but the branding still differed.\n\nThe admin portal overrides --primary with its own blue accent, and the sidebar\nheader renders in text-primary, so \"Admin Hub\" was blue while \"ProjectHub\" was\nnear-black. The accent is mirrored onto .client-portal [data-sidebar=\"sidebar\"]\n(light and dark) so both headers match. It is scoped to the sidebar rather than\n.client-portal so public pages keep their inherited near-black primary and\nnothing outside the sidebar shifts.\n\nApp.tsx also passed `md:opacity-100 opacity-0` to AppSidebar for a fade-in.\nThat class did nothing: useIsMobile() is JS matchMedia, so below 768px the\nsidebar renders through Sheet, whose branch does not forward `className` to\nSheetContent, and at 768px and above `md:opacity-100` wins the cascade. It was\nleftover from an earlier fade-in and is removed rather than kept as an\ninvitation to re-introduce a mobile bug. It was also the only reason AppSidebar\ntook a className prop, so the prop goes with it - one definition, one call site.\n\nThe minifier folds the identical light-mode blocks into\n`.admin-portal,.client-portal [data-sidebar=sidebar]`, which is the intended\nmerge and present in the built stylesheet.\n\ntsc and vite build are clean; the built CSS was checked directly for the new\nrule.","tree":{"sha":"271d53078fda34cec1feaaa9ad46df2eff42c31f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/trees/271d53078fda34cec1feaaa9ad46df2eff42c31f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/commits/30cf93e751a8fb245f8e9d804dd8747880aced73","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/30cf93e751a8fb245f8e9d804dd8747880aced73","node_id":"C_kwDOPjAFOtoAKDMwY2Y5M2U3NTFhOGZiMjQ1ZjhlOWQ4MDRkZDg3NDc4ODBhY2VkNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748","sha":"b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748"}],"sha":"30cf93e751a8fb245f8e9d