pe":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748","node_id":"C_kwDOPjAFOtoAKGI0MzdkNTU4YWMzZDQzZjc3ZmIxYTEyNWI0OWQ4ZjFjM2MzYzk3NDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/8ae5b4760bee3561f83594adfbbf074ac3a9eeba","sha":"8ae5b4760bee3561f83594adfbbf074ac3a9eeba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/8ae5b4760bee3561f83594adfbbf074ac3a9eeba"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commit/24c6904d45d0506b8efe3fd59dc319f6127a47c9","sha":"24c6904d45d0506b8efe3fd59dc319f6127a47c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/24c6904d45d0506b8efe3fd59dc319f6127a47c9"}],"sha":"b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/b437d558ac3d43f77fb1a125b49d8f1c3c3c9748"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175740463?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/openhands-agent","id":175740463,"login":"openhands-agent","node_id":"U_kgDOCnmWLw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openhands-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/commits/24c6904d45d0506b8efe3fd59dc319f6127a47c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:01:45Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:02:09Z","email":"openhands@all-hands.dev","name":"openhands"},"message":"Report database failures instead of a false-healthy /api/health\n\nGET /api/health returned 200 unconditionally, so a deployment whose\nDATABASE_URL was wrong still reported \"API is functioning properly\" while every\nquery failed with 28P01. Diagnosing a broken database meant reading server logs\ninstead of calling the endpoint.\n\nThe health check now issues SELECT 1 through storage.checkConnection() and\nreturns 503 with a short summary when the database is unusable.\n\ndescribeDbError could not classify those failures either: Drizzle wraps driver\nerrors in a DrizzleQueryError and keeps the original PostgresError on `cause`,\nso reading only the outermost `code` fell through to \"Database request failed\"\nfor every database-level error, including the authentication rejection that\nmatters most. findDbErrorCode walks the cause chain, so 28P01 now reports\n\"Database rejected the configured credentials\" while the raw error - which\ncarries the SQL text, bound parameters and connection string - stays in the\nserver log.\n\nVerified against a working database (200, database: connected) and one with\nrejected credentials (503, \"Database rejected the configured credentials\"),\nwith no SQL, host, role or stack frames in either response. tsc and vite build\nare clean.","tree":{"sha":"2155645d9e26d7dcd5e82ff66612f5329ed4fc5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/trees/2155645d9e26d7dcd5e82ff66612f5329ed4fc5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ProjectHub-fie/ProjectHub/git/commits/24c6904d45d0506b8efe3fd59dc319f6127a47c9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","sig